cookbook/references/index.md:21:- [[evaluation-and-truncation-follow-the-kaggriculture-objective|Evaluation and truncation follow the Kaggriculture objective]] — Tasks 3.2/3.3: raw-bank evaluation winners, economic reward kept on truncation, joint per-player clipping and value-mode guards, a per-evaluation seed in a checked int64 band (distinct per step within a run, not a global stream separator) and promotion telemetry logged after promotion completes; proven on the trainer seam (CPU TDD, fake env, 1,344 Python passes); since the Task 3.4 merge the guards run through the registered Kaggriculture env config and every `configs/kaggriculture*.yaml`; native env and a real Kaggriculture run pending.
cookbook/references/index.md:23:- [[v3-launchers-fail-fast-without-wandb-credentials|v3 launchers fail fast without W&B credentials]] — `run_ppo` defaults to online W&B in `kg-v3`, grouped by experiment id. Rank 0 fails fast before config load without a key. Offline or debug needs an explicit flag, prints a loud banner and is recorded with source commit and config hash in `attempts.jsonl`. `owl.train.logging` extends Isaiah's loggers so other launchers can reuse them. CPU tests with W&B doubles; BC has not adopted it yet.
cookbook/workflows/index.md:4:- [[install-the-wandb-credential-before-any-pod-launch|Install the W&B credential before any pod launch]] — Pod setup: copy only the api.wandb.ai netrc entry via stdin, chmod 600, check `wandb.Api()`, then launch online in `kg-v3`; an outage needs an explicit flag, a banner, an `attempts.jsonl` record and an owner report. Simulated locally on synthetic files; it has not run on a pod yet.
