# Independent audit/docs verification (subtask)

Reviewed `faed717..05cbd88` in `/Users/poonszesen/kg-v3-wandb`; no tracked edits, no real credential reads, no W&B network, no training/GPU. Scratch: `/private/tmp/verify-wandb-r1-audit/`.

## Findings

- **P2 — Credential filter can forward unrelated credentials.** `cookbook/workflows/install-the-wandb-credential-before-any-pod-launch.md:20` assumes entry boundaries occur at the start of a physical line. netrc is token-based: synthetic valid `machine api.wandb.ai login user password synthetic-wandb default login user password synthetic-default` is accepted by Python `netrc`, but the documented awk forwards both W&B and default credentials. Replacing the trailing default with `machine other.example ...` forwards the other machine too. The suggested grep count still reads one W&B header, so it cannot detect this. A valid `machine` newline `api.wandb.ai` input extracts nothing. Fix: parse netrc and select the exact `hosts['api.wandb.ai']` entry (not default-falling-back `authenticators`), safely serialize only that entry to SSH stdin, validate extraction before creating the destination; add synthetic tests for packed and split token layouts.
- **P3 — Slurm gate timing and inventory are imprecise.** `ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/wandb-audit.md:14` says credential failure occurs "before sbatch work". The guard is inside the submitted `.sbatch` at lines 234–247, after allocation; `launch_scaling_experiments.sh`, `launch_scaling_5090.sh`, and `launch_truncation_experiments.sh` call sbatch first and are omitted from the table. `launch-interactive.sh` is also omitted, though it only opens an interactive shell (and warns if the env file is absent). Fix: group/list these wrappers and state the credential check happens before container/trainer startup inside the allocated job.

## Checks

- `git status --short` initially/finally empty. `git log --oneline faed717..HEAD` contains one commit, `05cbd88`.
- `git diff --exit-code faed717..HEAD -- scripts/benchmark_checkpoints.py scripts/benchmark_envs.py scripts/slurm <six ops probe paths>` exited 0: audited tools/probes unchanged.
- Static inspection of baseline `python/owl/train/logging.py`/`scripts/run_ppo.py` confirms project orbit-wars, config/run directory/env/model/optimizer before logger, no telemetry guard.
- Read all three Slurm experiment wrappers, launch-train, smoke_scaling, launch-interactive; inspected both benchmark tools. Both benchmarks remain Orbit-only. No additional v3 training launcher found in the reviewed integration scope. The ops table groups all six specified probe families; they have no W&B references. Hash custody exists (flash manifest nested under pod; GEMM uses sha256*.txt rather than MANIFEST.sha256).
- `git show kg/rebuild-bc-trainer:scripts/train_bc.py` and `git show kg/rebuild-bc-trainer:python/owl/train/bc.py` only: branch resolves `b626f24e203205dadaacf32018c84edc06030522`. Confirms kg-v3 project, bc-bc name, group bc, online default, silent offline at launcher level, no telemetry field in attempt receipts. Main ordering: dataset 118, attempt 143, model 157, compile 158, optimizer 165, logger 175. BC imports remain available; MetricLogger is non-abstract, so BCWandbLogger/_NoopLogger need not implement the new method until adopting record_attempt. No BC source was edited.
- Added Reference and Workflow both have type/title/description/tags/status/generated, first tag kaggriculture-v3. All fourteen declared repository sources exist. Both indexes and prepended log link the new notes. README broadly matches scoped behavior and BC limitations are explicit in notes.
- Existing prepare log is green full prepare: ruff/format, Python 3.11 syntax, mypy 64 source files, docs lint, root Rust 254 passed/4 ignored, engine 69 passed, Python 1718 passed/11 skipped, docs-fresh, final EXIT=0. It contains this worktree path and expected test counts, but no explicit tested source SHA; final-source provenance is therefore implicit rather than cryptographically pinned. Parent performs independent py-prepare.
- `OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 python3 /private/tmp/verify-wandb-r1-audit/workflow_probe.py`: six synthetic checks; three pass, three fail. Passes: one-entry-per-line extraction with default dropped; ordinary multiline extraction with default dropped; local equivalent install yields 600, second install exits 1 and leaves original bytes unchanged. Failures: same-line next machine retained; same-line default retained; split machine/hostname dropped. Script/JSON evidence retained here. Only synthetic values, no real HOME/netrc access. SSH install body tested locally by replacing destination `$HOME/.netrc` token with scratch pathname, never running SSH.

