+++ b//private/tmp/verify-wandb-r1/report-suffix.md
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+
+**Audit and preserved semantics**
+
+- Baseline `faed717` uses project `orbit-wars`, lacks a telemetry gate/receipt, and opens its logger after config/run-directory/env/model setup. HEAD extends the shared logging module and canonical PPO trainer; it does not create another trainer.
+- `scripts/benchmark_checkpoints.py`, `scripts/benchmark_envs.py`, `scripts/slurm/*`, and all six named ops-probe families are byte-unchanged from the baseline. Both benchmarks remain Orbit-only; the frozen GPU checks, value gap, model SPS ceiling, GEMM limits, ATEN GEMM A/B, and flash-attn probes keep local evidence, with no W&B use. This is not completion of W&B adoption across all future launchers; the audit records the remaining work. Slurm precision is finding 7.
+- Read-only `git show kg/rebuild-bc-trainer:scripts/train_bc.py` and `git show kg/rebuild-bc-trainer:python/owl/train/bc.py`, resolving branch `b626f24e203205dadaacf32018c84edc06030522`, confirm project `kg-v3`, name `bc-bc`, group `bc`, online default, silent launcher-level offline selection, and no telemetry-mode receipt field. `main` loads the dataset (line 118), records an attempt (143), creates the model (157), compiles (158), and builds the optimizer (165) before logger construction (175). The late credential-failure claim is supported.
+- BC's current imports remain present. `MetricLogger` is not an ABC; adding `wandb_run_facts` does not break existing subclasses until they adopt `record_attempt`. No BC source was edited or runtime-tested.
+- AST comparisons confirm unchanged `LogMode`, `MetricLogger.close`, debug log/summary/close, W&B log/summary/close, `_logger_session`, `_resume_wandb_run_id`, and `_NoopLogger`. Checkpoint W&B ID handling and strict init `id`/`resume='must'` forwarding are retained. Failure-closing session and worker-no-logger tests pass.
+- The credential gate is rank-0-only. The conditional git lookup is also rank-0-only. An independent worker `main` probe replaces credentials/git access with failures and reaches the config boundary without either access. The existing worker-session test confirms no logger/final checkpoint. No model input, observation/history, actor/critic, or opponent-identity path changed.
+- At HEAD the telemetry gate precedes `FullConfig.from_file` and run-directory creation; a direct independent config sentinel confirms this. Launch resolution still precedes the gate, and directory-resume resolution can inspect checkpoints; this was not moved by the change.
+- A netrc `default` password is accepted by both the implementation and installed SDK. That is a real fallback, despite the narrower “host entry” prose. Missing-scheme URLs are rejected when the gate reaches host parsing, but not when a nonempty environment key bypasses it. Empty-string API key plus a valid netrc works in both; whitespace-only API key does not behave equivalently. Online/offline logger facts do not independently expose actual transport mode; `record_attempt` verifies W&B-present versus disabled, while logger construction selects online/offline from the identity.
+- No ordinary environment API key or netrc password was found flowing into config, receipts, summaries, stdout, or stderr. The URL-error exception in finding 4 prevents an unconditional claim that secrets can never reach stderr. Only synthetic markers were used to demonstrate it.
+
+**Documentation and preparation evidence**
+
+README matches the normal new flags, project/group, rank-0 gate, and receipt behavior; offline resume needs the qualification in finding 6. The new Reference and Workflow have complete required frontmatter and `kaggriculture-v3` as the first tag. All **14** declared repository sources exist. Both folder indexes and the prepended cookbook log link the new notes. The notes explicitly scope CPU test doubles, no pod/GPU qualification, the missing Kaggriculture environment, and BC's pending adoption. The Reference's independent-verification glob is a pending output location at this reviewed HEAD, not evidence of an earlier approval.
+
+`ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/wandb-2026-09-29/prepare.log` is a green recorded **full `just prepare`**: final `EXIT=0`, root Rust **254 passed / 4 ignored**, engine **69 passed**, Python **1,718 passed / 11 skipped**, formatting/lint/docs checks, Python 3.11 syntax, and mypy on **64** files. It identifies this worktree and matching counts but does not embed the tested commit hash, so exact final-source custody is implicit. The independent current `py-prepare` reproduces its Python result. No Rust run was repeated. Historical live W&B API observations written in the docs were not repeated because this verification is hermetic.
+
+**Restoration proof**
+
+Every initial, extra, and supplemental mutation is restored. Final byte comparisons prove scratch == worktree == `git show HEAD:<path>`:
+
+- `python/owl/train/logging.py`: SHA-256 `88c9cf53996b80411dd3cf2f1478cb39b0b76cca1de69c755f8f78b84fd9ddaa`.
+- `scripts/run_ppo.py`: SHA-256 `56f7dc634b547e4cfdedce32c6c9c90b59d8584ea21f1e4d42e0f84cfe4f816c`.
+
+`git diff --exit-code` and `git diff --cached --exit-code` both exit 0. Final `git status --short` is empty. Raw results, failed-test names, mutation definitions, logs, and restoration proof remain in temporary evidence directories only. No commit or push.
+
+VERDICT: REQUEST CHANGES
